summary:
  The sync engine reports a finished calibration through app.notifyy, a
  function main.qml does not have.

history:
  SyncEngine.qml reaches the widget through `app`, a `property var` that
  main.qml binds to its root, and FullRepresentation.qml reaches it through
  main.qml's id. qmllint knows the type behind neither name: a member that
  does not exist, planted behind `root.` in FullRepresentation.qml and
  behind `app.` in SyncEngine.qml on 2026-11-12, got no message of its own
  in the JSON report and the lint stayed green. In a
  binding such a read is undefined without a word; in a handler the call
  throws the first time its branch runs, here when a calibration has
  succeeded. tests/test_cross_file_members.py follows the names by the code
  that wires the files together: 1559 reads on the day it was written.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
  app.notify(i18n("Speakers calibrated"), calText, "audio-input-microphone");

replace:
  app.notifyy(i18n("Speakers calibrated"), calText, "audio-input-microphone");

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cross_file_members.py::test_the_shipped_files_read_no_member_that_is_not_there,
  which names the line, the name and ui/main.qml.
